📚 Online Bookstore Database Management System – SQL Project
This project is based on an Online Bookstore database system where data is stored, managed and analyzed using SQL & MySQL. In this version I grew the dataset to 1,000 customers and 1,000 orders and added Payment Method and Platform details, so the analysis has a lot more to show.
The project includes: 
✔️ Database schema design
✔️ CSV dataset import
✔️ Table relationships using Primary & Foreign Keys
✔️ Data analysis queries
✔️ Sales & inventory insights
✔️ Payment method & platform analysis (new)
📁 Dataset Files
The project uses three CSV files:
•	Books.csv – 500 books (Book_ID 1 to 500)
•	Customers.csv – 1,000 customers (Customer_ID 1 to 1,000)
•	Orders.csv – 1,000 orders (Order_ID 1 to 1,000), from 09 Dec 2022 to 07 Dec 2024
📝 Quick note: customers 501–1,000 and orders 501–1,000 are simulated records I added to grow the data, and Payment_Method & Platform were assigned randomly. So this is practice data, not real sales.
🗄 Database Tables
🟦 Books Table
Stores book-related data such as: Book_ID, Title, Author, Genre, Published_Year, Price, Stock
🟩 Customers Table
Stores customer details: Customer_ID, Name, Email, Phone, City, Country, Payment_Method, Platform
🟨 Orders Table
Stores transaction records: Order_ID, Customer_ID, Book_ID, Order_Date, Quantity, Total_Amount
💳 New Columns in Customers Table
•	Payment_Method → Online, Offline, Cash, Card
•	Platform → Amazon, Flipkart, Meesho, Myntra, Ajio
🔗 Table Relationships (Keys)
•	Book_ID → Links Books & Orders
•	Customer_ID → Links Customers & Orders
✔️ Ensures referential integrity
✔️ Avoids duplicate & inconsistent data
✔️ All 1,000 orders point to a valid customer and book
